        role: "Neighbor with the doorbell camera",
        exam: [.direct("What happened to your truck?", "\"My pickup, parked on the street, was found in the morning with a smashed windshield and a torn-off mirror.\""), .direct("What was the damage?", "\"About nine hundred dollars for a new windshield and a mirror, plus a day of work.\""), .direct("What does your doorbell camera show?", "\"A person with a bat swinging at the truck, smashing the glass, and running toward the corner.\""), .direct("What was found nearby?", "\"A bat with glass chips, in a hedge two houses down, which deputies took as evidence.\""), .direct("Why do you suspect {DL}?", "\"{DL} had argued with me over parking just before this happened, and had threatened me.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say?", "\"{D.He} said {D.he} was across town at a friend's house that night.\""), .cross("The person's face isn't visible?", "\"No, the face isn't visible, because a hood covered it and the picture is dark.\""), .cross("The bat could belong to anyone?", "\"Yes, but it was found near the route the figure ran.\""), .cross("{DL} lives nearby?", "\"{D.He} lives on the next street over, which is close enough to run from.\""), .cross("You've argued with {DL} before?", "\"Yes, we've argued before, over a parking spot, many times over the past year.\""), .cross("{DL} has an alibi?", "\"{D.He} says so, but I don't know of any witness, other than {D.his} friends.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} smashed a neighbor's truck.", "A neighbor who was somewhere else."),
        allocution: "\"I was at my friend's house that night, and I did not smash that truck. We argued about parking, and I'm sorry that things got heated. I'd never destroy someone's windshield and mirror. I hope the person who did it is found, and I'd ask the court to speak to my friend.\"",
