        defendant: [.direct("Did you use your neighbor's card without permission?", "\"No. {V.He} told me to use it. {V.He} gave me the code and said to buy {V.his} medicine and a few gifts.\""), .direct("When did {V.he} tell you that?", "\"A few days before, when {V.he} was sick and couldn't leave the house. {V.He} asked me to run errands.\""), .direct("Why did you buy gift cards?", "\"{V.He} asked for gift cards for {V.his} grandchildren's birthdays, and I bought them as {V.he} asked.\""), .direct("Did you buy anything for yourself?", "\"A few items I needed, and I told {V.him} I'd pay {V.him} back. I should have asked first.\""), .direct("What did you do when you learned the card was reported lost?", "\"I went to {V.him} and offered to return everything I had left.\""), .direct("What would you tell your neighbor?", "\"I'm sorry for the confusion. I thought I had permission, and I'll repay every dollar.\""), .cross("You've been charged with using someone else's card before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I told the judge last time that I would change, and I meant it. I should have gotten {V.his} permission in writing.\""), .cross("{V.He} says {V.he} never gave you permission?", "\"{V.He} does, and I understand why {V.he}'s upset, since {V.he}'s elderly and confused at times.\""), .cross("You used a lost card three times in one visit?", "\"I did, and I can see how that looks to the store and the court.\""), .cross("You'll repay the six hundred twenty dollars?", "\"Yes, in full, on a schedule that the court sets for me.\""), .cross("You'll stay away from {V.his} cards and {V.his} accounts?", "\"Yes, I won't touch {V.his} cards or {V.his} accounts again, and I'll keep away from anything of {V.hers}.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, an older neighbor, reported $620 in drugstore purchases made with a debit card {V} had lost, and store video showed {D} at the register, and this was not {DL}'s first time here, after {PRIOR} in {PRIORDATE}.", "The defense will say {V} had given {D} the card to buy medicine, and {D} used it for the purpose it was given. {D} did not take a lost card."),
