        truths: ("{DL} had a prior case in this court and used part of the $60,000 for a boat payment.", "A co-op filing exists in {DL}'s name but was never funded or opened."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you take your victim's money?", "\"I took sixty thousand dollars for a co-op I was planning to start. I meant to invest it.\""), .direct("Why did you call it guaranteed?", "\"I believed it would succeed, and I wanted {V.him} to feel safe. I shouldn't have used that word.\""), .direct("Where did the money go?", "\"Into my account, and I used some for the co-op's start-up costs and some for my own bills.\""), .direct("Why hasn't the co-op opened?", "\"It's been slow. I couldn't find land at the right price, and I ran short of funds.\""), .direct("Did you plan to cheat him?", "\"No. I planned to build something good and pay {V.him} back. I got in over my head.\""), .direct("What would you tell him and his son?", "\"I'm sorry for the loss and the worry. I'll repay every dollar I can.\""), .cross("You've been convicted of investment fraud before, haven't you?", "\"Yes, and I said I would tell the truth in my dealings, and I didn't. I shouldn't have promised a guarantee.\""), .cross("You deposited a retiree's money in your personal checking account?", "\"I did deposit a retiree's money into my own account, and I know how that looks.\""), .cross("You told him there was no risk?", "\"I did tell {V.him} there was no risk, and that wasn't true.\""), .cross("You'll repay sixty thousand dollars?", "\"I'll repay what I can, on a plan that the court and the family accept.\""), .cross("You'll stop selling investments?", "\"Yes, I'll stop selling investments, and I'll hand back every document I have.\"")],
        openings: ("{V}, a retiree, handed {D} $60,000 for a 'guaranteed' investment in a farm co-op, and no co-op existed, and the money went into {D}'s checking account, and {DL} had faced this court in {PRIORDATE} over {PRIOR}.", "The defense will say the co-op was real and delayed, and {D} meant to deliver the returns. A delay in a co-op is not a fraud."),
