        theory: ("{D} sold a flood car as clean.", "A dealer who did not know."),
        allocution: "\"I bought that sedan at an auction, and it looked clean. The only thing I did was wash it. I did not know it had been in a hurricane. I'm sorry to {V}, who paid seven thousand five hundred dollars. I'll make it right, and I'll check history reports before I sell anything.\"",
